110
00:06:33,058 --> 00:06:35,058
Kuja, set sail for Ruskaina!

111
00:06:35,058 --> 00:06:37,058
Aye, aye, Snake Princess!

112
00:06:46,058 --> 00:06:48,058
This island will be perfect.

113
00:06:48,058 --> 00:06:53,058
It has 48 seasons a year, so you'll constantly have to adapt to the harsh conditions.

114
00:06:54,058 --> 00:06:55,058
Whoa!

115
00:06:55,058 --> 00:06:56,058
Sounds neat!

116
00:06:59,058 --> 00:07:00,058
Oh, Luffy!

117
00:07:01,058 --> 00:07:06,058
While you're here, I'll be sure to bring you the most delicious food from Amazon Lily every day.

118
00:07:06,058 --> 00:07:07,058
Doesn't that sound nice?

119
00:07:08,058 --> 00:07:09,058
Yeah!

120
00:07:09,058 --> 00:07:10,058
Thanks, Hancock!

121
00:07:10,058 --> 00:07:11,058
You rock!

122
00:07:11,058 --> 00:07:14,058
Let's see, could you start off with that specialty gorgon something or other?

123
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:15,058
That stuff's really good.

124
00:07:16,058 --> 00:07:17,058
Why, yes, of course!

125
00:07:18,058 --> 00:07:19,058
Yay!

126
00:07:19,058 --> 00:07:20,058
That's our princess!

127
00:07:20,058 --> 00:07:24,058
I'll bring you anything you desire, and as much of it as you want.

128
00:07:25,058 --> 00:07:26,058
Oh, my!

129
00:07:26,058 --> 00:07:29,058
I do believe he's uttered my name at least ten times now.

130
00:07:32,058 --> 00:07:34,058
That must mean we're engaged!

131
00:07:34,058 --> 00:07:35,058
No, it doesn't!

132
00:07:35,058 --> 00:07:38,058
And didn't you say a little while ago that you were married?

133
00:07:39,058 --> 00:07:42,058
Foolish girl doesn't even know the proper order of things.

134
00:07:42,058 --> 00:07:43,058
No, Hancock.

135
00:07:43,058 --> 00:07:46,058
Sorry, but I just can't have you spoiling him.

136
00:07:46,058 --> 00:07:48,058
His sole purpose here is to train.

137
00:07:48,058 --> 00:07:50,058
He can't let distractions get in the way.

138
00:07:51,058 --> 00:07:52,058
What?

139
00:07:52,058 --> 00:07:53,058
Huh?

140
00:07:53,058 --> 00:07:54,058
You have got some nerve, old man.

141
00:07:54,058 --> 00:07:56,058
Luffy has the right to decide that.

142
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:57,058
You got it!

143
00:07:57,058 --> 00:07:59,058
And be careful how you respond.

144
00:07:59,058 --> 00:08:01,058
I can turn you to stone!

145
00:08:01,058 --> 00:08:03,058
There are plenty of things to eat here.

146
00:08:03,058 --> 00:08:05,058
Luffy needs to hunt for himself.

147
00:08:05,058 --> 00:08:06,058
That's part of the training.

148
00:08:06,058 --> 00:08:09,058
You'll ruin his nose, Snake Princess!

149
00:08:09,058 --> 00:08:14,058
If he can't get by with roughing it for a while, then maybe he shouldn't be a pirate.

150
00:08:14,058 --> 00:08:16,058
This is all for Luffy's benefit.

151
00:08:16,058 --> 00:08:17,058
Huh?

152
00:08:18,058 --> 00:08:19,058
Luffy?

153
00:08:19,058 --> 00:08:21,058
Then this will help him become stronger.

154
00:08:21,058 --> 00:08:23,058
Yes, it will.

155
00:08:23,058 --> 00:08:25,058
If this is all for Luffy.

156
00:08:27,058 --> 00:08:29,058
Then I'll be patient!

157
00:08:29,058 --> 00:08:30,058
Mm-hmm.

158
00:08:30,058 --> 00:08:33,058
But Rayleigh, this island is truly dangerous.

159
00:08:33,058 --> 00:08:35,058
If anything should happen to him.

160
00:08:35,058 --> 00:08:38,058
That's why it's an ideal place to train him.

161
00:08:38,058 --> 00:08:41,058
If you're that worried, make a wish on a star.

162
00:08:41,058 --> 00:08:43,058
Are you ready, Luffy?

163
00:08:43,058 --> 00:08:44,058
Sure am!

164
00:08:46,058 --> 00:08:49,058
Goodbye, Luffy! It's been fun!

165
00:08:49,058 --> 00:08:50,058
Don't get killed, okay?

166
00:08:50,058 --> 00:08:52,058
Bye!

167
00:08:52,058 --> 00:08:55,058
Luffy, take care of yourself.

168
00:08:55,058 --> 00:09:04,058
You'd better remember this tree.

169
00:09:06,058 --> 00:09:09,058
Even the most savage beasts stay away from it.

170
00:09:09,058 --> 00:09:12,058
It's the only safe area on this island.

171
00:09:12,058 --> 00:09:14,058
I don't think I'll forget it.

172
00:09:14,058 --> 00:09:16,058
It's pretty funny looking.

173
00:09:25,058 --> 00:09:31,058
And another thing to know, you may have guessed, but we're the only humans on this entire island.

174
00:09:32,058 --> 00:09:34,058
Behold the vast wilderness.

175
00:09:34,058 --> 00:09:37,058
Supposedly there was a country here a long time ago.

176
00:09:37,058 --> 00:09:40,058
But as you can see, the humans lost the struggle for survival.

177
00:09:40,058 --> 00:09:44,058
The land is rough, and nature relentless.

178
00:09:44,058 --> 00:09:45,058
Oh!

179
00:10:05,058 --> 00:10:07,058
This place smells like adventure!

180
00:10:14,058 --> 00:10:17,058
The island is crawling with vicious creatures.

181
00:10:17,058 --> 00:10:19,058
Far too many to be counted.

182
00:10:19,058 --> 00:10:25,058
Now, by my estimation, there's about 500 animals you don't stand a chance of defeating yet.

183
00:10:25,058 --> 00:10:29,058
Unless you become stronger, you might even get killed in your sleep.

184
00:10:29,058 --> 00:10:31,058
How do you know so much about this place?

185
00:10:31,058 --> 00:10:33,058
Did you used to live here?

186
00:10:33,058 --> 00:10:35,058
Yes, as you will.

187
00:10:35,058 --> 00:10:38,058
And you'll obtain the same power I did then.

188
00:10:38,058 --> 00:10:39,058
Huh?

189
00:10:39,058 --> 00:10:42,058
The power known as hockey.

190
00:10:44,058 --> 00:10:45,058
Hockey.

191
00:10:53,058 --> 00:10:54,058
Hey, watch out!

192
00:10:54,058 --> 00:10:56,058
There's a huge thing behind you!

193
00:10:56,058 --> 00:10:57,058
What are you doing?

194
00:10:57,058 --> 00:10:58,058
Don't just stand there!

195
00:10:58,058 --> 00:11:00,058
Listen to me, Luffy.

196
00:11:00,058 --> 00:11:04,058
Believe it or not, hockey is a latent power that everyone has within themselves.

197
00:11:04,058 --> 00:11:05,058
Wow!

198
00:11:05,058 --> 00:11:07,058
I think it's a giant elephant!

199
00:11:07,058 --> 00:11:10,058
Like five times the normal size!

200
00:11:10,058 --> 00:11:11,058
Observation.

201
00:11:11,058 --> 00:11:12,058
Fighting spirit.

202
00:11:12,058 --> 00:11:13,058
Intimidation.

203
00:11:13,058 --> 00:11:18,058
Hockey is really no different from any combative instincts normal humans have.

204
00:11:20,058 --> 00:11:24,058
However, most of them live their lives without tapping into their true potential,

205
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:27,058
because they don't have a teacher like you do now.

206
00:11:30,058 --> 00:11:32,058
You mustn't have any self-doubt.

207
00:11:32,058 --> 00:11:34,058
Only then will you become stronger.

208
00:11:35,058 --> 00:11:37,058
Run away!

209
00:11:39,058 --> 00:11:41,058
Time for second gear!

210
00:11:41,058 --> 00:11:42,058
Jetcastle!

211
00:11:51,058 --> 00:11:52,058
Damn it!

212
00:11:52,058 --> 00:11:53,058
This guy's no joke!

213
00:11:53,058 --> 00:11:55,058
He's super fast for as big as he is!

214
00:11:55,058 --> 00:12:01,058
Now watch very carefully.

215
00:12:01,058 --> 00:12:04,058
There are two prominent types of hockey used in battle.

216
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,058
Get out of there!

217
00:12:07,058 --> 00:12:08,058
Don't worry.

218
00:12:08,058 --> 00:12:12,058
The elephant will try to hit me with its trunk coming in from the right side.

219
00:12:12,058 --> 00:12:21,058
First is the power to feel the presence of others more strongly.

220
00:12:21,058 --> 00:12:23,058
This is known as observation hut.

221
00:12:27,058 --> 00:12:28,058
No way!

222
00:12:28,058 --> 00:12:33,058
If you enhance this power, you can even tell where unseen enemies are located.

223
00:12:34,058 --> 00:12:37,058
You can determine how many there are and predict what their next moves will be.

224
00:12:38,058 --> 00:12:39,058
Really?

225
00:12:39,058 --> 00:12:40,058
That left kick won't work.

226
00:12:41,058 --> 00:12:42,058
Mantra.

227
00:12:42,058 --> 00:12:43,058
Mantra.

228
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:49,058
On Skypiea, it has a different name.

229
00:12:49,058 --> 00:12:51,058
There, it's called Mantra.

230
00:12:53,058 --> 00:12:54,058
Oh!

231
00:12:54,058 --> 00:12:55,058
Dammit!

232
00:12:56,058 --> 00:12:57,058
Next, the armor mataki.

233
00:12:58,058 --> 00:13:01,058
Think of it as covering yourself in invisible armor.

234
00:13:05,058 --> 00:13:06,058
Riley, no!

235
00:13:06,058 --> 00:13:07,058
No!

236
00:13:18,058 --> 00:13:19,058
That move!

237
00:13:19,058 --> 00:13:20,058
I've seen it before!

238
00:13:20,058 --> 00:13:21,058
Has she got it, Dokoi?

239
00:13:26,058 --> 00:13:29,058
Armor that's hard enough can even be used as a weapon.

240
00:13:33,058 --> 00:13:34,058
Hey!

241
00:13:34,058 --> 00:13:35,058
I shouldn't be able to feel that!

242
00:13:35,058 --> 00:13:36,058
I made out a rubber!

243
00:13:36,058 --> 00:13:40,058
Consider it another benefit of knowing how to use this haki.

244
00:13:41,058 --> 00:13:45,058
Unless they have a specific weak point, those with devil fruit powers are hard to hit.

245
00:13:46,058 --> 00:13:50,058
Armament haki provides the only other effective countermeasure against such enemies.

246
00:13:53,058 --> 00:13:56,058
Take those with logia-type devil fruits.

247
00:13:56,058 --> 00:13:59,058
Their body composition makes them seem impossible to touch,

248
00:13:59,058 --> 00:14:02,058
but armament haki has the power to strike them.

249
00:14:02,058 --> 00:14:04,058
Ah, so that's how you were able to hit Kizaru.

250
00:14:05,058 --> 00:14:06,058
Interesting.

251
00:14:06,058 --> 00:14:11,058
That kind of haki might be able to punch Smokey or Aokiji or anybody.

252
00:14:15,058 --> 00:14:18,058
You can also transfer armament haki to a weapon.

253
00:14:19,058 --> 00:14:21,058
Have you ever seen the Kuja Pirate's arrows?

254
00:14:21,058 --> 00:14:22,058
I have.

255
00:14:24,058 --> 00:14:27,058
It was like they were made out of steel.

256
00:14:28,058 --> 00:14:30,058
Observation and armament.

257
00:14:31,058 --> 00:14:33,058
They're the two main types of haki.

258
00:14:34,058 --> 00:14:39,058
However, there are some people in this world who can use another type of haki.

259
00:14:40,058 --> 00:14:41,058
Watch closely.

260
00:14:41,058 --> 00:14:45,058
Huh?

261
00:14:48,058 --> 00:14:49,058
Huh?

262
00:14:54,058 --> 00:14:56,058
Huh?

263
00:14:57,058 --> 00:14:58,058
Huh?

264
00:14:58,058 --> 00:15:03,058
Huh?

265
00:15:03,058 --> 00:15:13,058
Uhr...

266
00:15:33,058 --> 00:15:46,938
The power to intimidate your enemies into submission.

267
00:15:47,578 --> 00:15:49,278
This is Conqueror's Hockey.

268
00:15:51,338 --> 00:15:54,278
The most well-known legends of the Grand Line.

269
00:15:54,858 --> 00:15:58,118
They often have the rare Conqueror's Hockey at their disposal.

270
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:02,518
However, although you can control the Conqueror's Hockey,

271
00:16:02,518 --> 00:16:05,758
unlike the other types, there's no way to train yourself to use it.

272
00:16:06,158 --> 00:16:09,218
The Conqueror's Hockey embodies the spirit of the owner himself.

273
00:16:09,578 --> 00:16:12,178
Strengthen your spirit and you strengthen its power.

274
00:16:12,398 --> 00:16:14,918
Hey! That's what you did at the auction house!

275
00:16:15,018 --> 00:16:16,458
